// Bech32 and bech32m, BIP 173 and BIP 350:
// https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0173.mediawiki
// https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0350.mediawiki
//
// This is how a public key becomes a string a person can read out loud
// (`age1…`) and how a secret key becomes one (`AGE-SECRET-KEY-1…`). The
// checksum is what makes a typo a refusal rather than a wrong key.
//
// Both variants live here because the two differ only in the constant the
// checksum is mixed with, and a decoder has to tell them apart to be useful:
// bech32m exists because bech32's checksum was found to miss the deletion of a
// final `q`.
//
// Not here: the segwit address rules built on top — witness versions, program
// lengths, the 8-to-5 padding rules of a script. This decodes the encoding, not
// the addresses.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/buffer",
}
